{"name":"Regency Rose","hex":"#a78881","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regency","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A system of government that substitutes for the reign of a king or queen when that king or queen becomes unable to rule.","The time during which a regent is in power."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regency"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Regent","blocks":[{"text":"In a monarchy, a regent is a person appointed to execute the office of a monarch temporarily, essentially as a substitute ruler. Regencies may arise for a number of reasons, including the monarch being a minor, ill, absent from the country, or otherwise unavailable. A regent may also be appointed in cases where the throne is vacant, or the identity of the legitimate monarch is disputed. The rule of a regent or regents is called a regency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif/lossless-page1-330px-Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regent"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif/lossless-page1-500px-Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif/lossless-page1-1280px-Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif/lossless-page1-500px-Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"16th century Swedish regent Stenonis Stur